#3518
englehardt lord spectre~
the &+Lspectre &nof &+rLord Englehardt&N~
The &+Lspectre&n of &+rLord Englehardt&n hovers here, guarding his vault.
~
The somber apparation of the lord of the manor, &+rVanis Englehardt&n hovers about
in this room painfully aware that the mistakes of his life cost his family and
countless others their lives.  The great conjurer, Vanis had continued the work
of his ancestors.  He, like his father and many before him, sought to extend
his life.  As humans, the Englehardts were jealous of such long living races
as the elves and mountain dwarves.  Their desire to increase their longevity
inevitably left them with an empty life and a failed sense of accomplishment.
Vanis, the most promising of the ancestors sought to find the answers that had
eluded the prior lords.  His failure and lack of judgment was the most severe
and cataclysmic of them all.  Vanis stands here, seeking to speak of his quest
for life, perhaps to alleviate his pain.
~
