&+bAn elderly &+gMoss&+cwood &+gvillage &+bwoman is here, talking with the others.&N
~
&+wLeaning against the tree where several village elders have gathered, this
&+wwoman looks to be well in her sixties or even seventies. Her hair has lost
&+wits original colour and is now a flecked grey, but it is still long and
&+whangs down the length of her neck. The lines around her nose, mouth and
&+weyes have etched deep over the many years of her life and her face is now
&+wwrinkled. The deepest of the grooves are laugh lines, so she still looks
&+wyoung in a certain sense. She is somewhat short and plump, and does not
&+wwear any jewelry or other trinkets. She is busy talking and does not look
&+wat you when you approach. Perhaps it is a daily ritual for them to meet.&N
~
