&+LHorseman of &+gPestilence&+L, champion of pain, delights at your presence.
~
&+g   Pestilence, like all of the Apocalypse demons, is obsessed with the
&+gdestruction of all life forms, including the insects which he commands.  The
&+gmonster is smart and resourceful, using both subterfuge and the direct approach
&+gin his dealings with the intelligent creatures.  He finds it especially
&+ggratifying to inflict suffering and death by disease, sickness, and starvation.
&+gFrom a distance, the demon resembles a robust, horned humanoid.  Upon closer
&+ginspection it looks like the body is covered with insects.  In actuality,
&+gPestilence is a ten foot tall, horned skeleton made of bone.  The apparent bulk
&+gof his entire body is composed of tens of thousands of living insects and
&+garachnids that he can unleash in great swarms.  It is the swarm of insects
&+gthat gives him the appearance of having great mass.  The types of bugs and
&+garachnids that compose this monster's body include biting flies, gnats,
&+gmosquitoes, ants, wasps, bees, a variety of beetles, grasshoppers, spiders,
&+gscorpions, and larvae.
~
