   Sitting wearily upon an ornate chair, the castle lord
contemplates his once grand castle and its importance in
defending the surrounding countryside from invasion.
Wearing an exquisitly gilded suit of armor, and badges of
his rank and status, he is more dressed for an occassion
of state, than that of contemplation.  Showing signs of
age, he is slumped forward, and whisps of white hair can
be seen from underneath his helm.

Looking up from his revere Du'Maathe says "Ah my friend,
you are either a very brave hero or a fool.  Which are
thee?".
~
