~
&+L   Once a handsome lord of a realm the spanned a years journed in every
&+Ldirection, Vathor was a kind and benevolent leige for scores of years.  In
&+Lthe twilight of his life, as his vanity and strength faded, Vathor began to
&+Lexperiment with forces powerful far beyond his comprehension in an effort
&+Lto extend his life and thereby his reign.  At first his motives were true
&+Lto his benevolent nature, as he knew he could lead his people far better
&+Lthan his spoiled and power hungry son.  Eventually however, ever so slightly,
&+Lthe rightousness of his pure heart grew poisoned with the shadow of evil,
&+Land terrible forces of destruction planted their seed deep within Vathor.
&+LHis soul now a fertile feeding ground for the hungry darkness within himself,
&+LVathor grew hateful and angry even as he succeeded at prolonging his life
&+Lthrough what he thought was magical experimentation.  Gradually his realms
&+Lshrunk and divided through bitter civil wars and the burdon of oppression,
&+Lthe ground around his very keep soaked with blood as his dungeons filled
&+Lto the breaking point with tortured peasants.  A thousand years of this
&+Lpassed before the evil presence which lived within Vathor grew tired of its
&+Lplaything, and performed the cruelest action of all, turning Vathors eyes
&+Lwithin and allowing him to see his true nature and what he had become.  In
&+La spasm of horror, Vathor reached deep within himself and found a single
&+Lminute speck of goodness hidden deep within his recesses, and reversed all
&+Lof the hatred and destruction he had sown with a single sacrafice.  Flashing
&+Lin the air with the song of a thousand weightless birds, his blade of justice
&+Lclutched within his hands, Vathor decapitated himself even as his kings death
&+Loath escaped his lips.  His final curse has sent him here, bodyless, to spend
&+Lthe rest of eternity drinking the blood of others and suffering the pain of
&+Ldecapitation, while his lands and people are now protected by his final wish.&n
~
