This old magician wears mouse colored robes. He bumbles on and looks ready to
trip over his own two feet mumbling something about a powerful magic spell
call fireball. "If only I could remember how it goes, fir.., fireturkey,
firemart, fir...." His pointy top hat looks nearly done in, with its fiber
nearly worn, a simple touch could unwind the entire thing. The robes flow
freely around his body, and he doesn't have a component belt for his spells.
His long flowing beard looks far too long for it drops just above his solar
plexus. The brow on his forehead are full of lines and wrinckles, this magi
is truly old, although his voice sounds vibrant and shows no signs of any
weakness, if it weren't for him talking nonsense that is. This man doesn't
seem affected by the outside world, as if too senile to realize that he's in
anykind of danger. But, perhaps there is more to this man than the image he
projects, perhaps there lies more under the mask than out.
