   &+rA man of noble birth, Strahd spent much of his life serving causes of
&+rgoodness and law, most notably as a warrior and leader of the Ravenloft
&+rarmies.  Years of such service took their toll upon him, however, and
&+rby the time he reached middle age, Strahd came to believe he had squan-
&+rdered his life and his youth.  With this dark mood upon him, he came to
&+rconquer &+LBarovia&+r, and assumed lordship over the entire realm.
&+rTaking as his residence permanently in the Castle he once fought to
&+rdefend, Strahd became the unquestioned ruler of Ravenloft.  From this
&+rposition of power and security, he called for members of his family
&+r"long unseated from their ancestral thrones" to join them, including
&+rhis younger brother named Sergei.  Some time after this reunion, the
&+rCount himself fell in love with a young Barovian woman, Tatyana,
&+rthough she rejected his affections in favor of the younger Sergei.
&+rFilled with despair and jealousy, and brooding a growing hatred for
&+rSergei, Strahd sought magical means to restore his youth.  In a moment of
&+rdesperate frustration, he made a pact with death - a pact of blood.  On the
&+rday of Sergei and Tatyana's wedding, Strahd murdered his brother and
&+rpursued the grieving Tatyana until she flung herself from the walls of
&+rRavenloft into the crag below.  Strahd himself was shot down by the arrows
&+rof the castle guard.  Even so, he did not die, but went on to rule the land
&+rof Barovia as the self-proclaimed First Vampire.
~
