#80736
yarguza worm~
&+ma hungry yarguza&N~
&+mA hungry worm chews its way through solid stone.&N
~
Despite its small size, the dreaded yarguza is a worm of insatiable
appetite possessing powerful jaws and a poisonous bite.  Miners of all
sorts hate and fear these worms.  The worms eat stone and metal, any
stone or metal, showing no preference or aversion to anything so long as
it is mineral.  It is rumored that their excrement itself can also melt
stone, and can weaken metal.
~
