#132631
kabanon prophet old man~
&+LKabanon&n, &+Wthe prophet&n~
&+yA diminutive &+Wold &+Lman&+y sits here, scribbling on some &+Wvellum&+y.&n
~
   Flesh as &+Lblack&n as charcoal, this old man sits here with a quill in one hand
and a pad of &+Wvellum&n in the other.  His skin hangs on his bones, as if added by
afterthought, its dark folds seeming to hide many wonderous things.  He has
short kinky &+Wwhite&n hair, a recessing widow's peak the most prominant feature of
his round melon head.  He pauses in his writing and looks up at you.

   '&+LBusy, busy, busy&n,' he mutters then returns to his work.

   '&+CWhat are you writing old man?&n' you reply, almost in jest.

   '&+LWhy, I'm writing about the end&n,' he grins stupidly in your face.

   '&+CThe end of what?&n' anger rises in your throat.

   '&+LThe end of the end, of course.  Would you like to buy a copy?  Or perhaps,
&+Lyou want a map?  I may have those, too&n,' Kabanon winks then looks back at his
pad.
~
