xero barbarian mercenary old large trapper~
&+yX&+We&+yr&+Yo&n, the &+Bbarbarian &+ymercenary&n~
A large &+Bbarbarian&n sits here, concentrating on building traps.
~
&n	This large barbarian hears your approach, but doesn't look up until he gets a spring
in place on his trap.  Turning to you he nods and extends his hand in greeting.

	&+W"Hello there.  I am &+yX&+We&+yr&+Yo, a barbarian &+Ymercenary&+W from Ugta.  I am
	&+Win town a few days to catch enough deer to last my family through the winter.
	&+WEven though I'm retired from adventuring, the &+Yskills&+W I learned when I was younger
	&+Wstill serve me well as a hunter for my family.

Suddenly his warm smiles fades as he begins to speak again.

	&+W"Have you met that idiot gnome next door yet?  I have never met anyone so conceited
	&+Win my life!  It would be one thing if he could back up half of the stories he tells,
	&+Wbut years ago my friends and I decided to bring him along for our trip through the
	&+WRift Jungle.  A conjurer is usually a nice bonus to any group, or so we thought.
	&+WThe fool charged ahead of us in every encounter and it was all we could do to keep
	&+Whim from getting himself killed.  When we stumbled upon a bullywug warparty, he
	&+Wcharged the chief, a mighty warrior, himself.  First making sure our other more
	&+Wresponsible casters were properly protected, I rushed to his defense just as the chief
	&+Whad laid him out with a mighty charge and was about to finish him off.  Even after I
	&+Wsaved him he seemed to not realize the danger he had put himself in and charged the
	&+Wnext closest target.  I have no idea how that fool is still alive."&n

&+yX&+We&+yr&+Yo&n sighs and shakes his head, then excuses himself after his stomache growls.

	&+W"Excuse me.  I've been here making traps all day and haven't breaked long enough
	&+Wto grab &+Ysomething to eat&n.  After a few more I might check and see if the
	&+Wkitchen is still open."&n
~
