leodra pudgy gnome conjurer idiot~
&+yL&+Ye&+Wo&+yd&+Yra&n, the pudgy &+Rgnome&n &+Yconjurer&n~
A pudgy &+Rgnome&n sulks while sitting at his desk.
~
	&+W"It is customary to knock and wait to be welcomed in you know.  Though I know
	&+Wit must be difficult for you youngsters to hear of my arrival and not know how
	&+Wto go about meeting me properly.  I am of course the great gnome conjurer, Leodra.
	&+WYou've heard of my endless travels and heroic feats I'm sure.  There mustn't be an
	&+Wurd or bullywug who hasn't heard my name and trembled with fear!  Those pesky
	&+Wdragons everyone carries on about must have heard my name as well, as I've never
	&+Wseen one dare to roam near this city while I'm around.  As long as they know not
	&+Wto come here, I see no reason why I should journey to their lairs and harass them."&n

He sighs and his frown grows even wider.

	&+W"I feel compelled to write my memoirs and share my vast knowledge with the world, yet
	&+Wit is proving difficult.  I tried to conjure a book big enough, but eighty pages hardly
	&+Wseems enough room to describe all my &+Yadventures&+W in any detail. Whatever shall I do?"&n

He sighs again, then seems to perk up while studying you.

	&+W"I wonder if you might be able to help me.  In one of the rooms near here is a library of
	&+Wsorts that the innkeeper has set up for us customers to browse during our stays.  I am
	&+Wsure that there must be some blank books hidden in there somewhere that he hasn't yet used
	&+Wto copy down more tales, possibly in the desk.  During my last visit the innkeeper
	&+Wfound a few books I had hid in my bag, that I had simply wished to borrow, and has forbade
	&+Wme from using his library again.  Perhaps you could go there in my stead, and &+Ysearch the
	&+Ydesk&+W for an unused book I could use.  If you could do that for me I'd be only too happy
	&+Wto give you the smaller book I conjured, and even autograph it for you!"&n
~
