statue old man~
&+La &nstatue &+Lof an o&nl&+Wd &+Cman&n~
&+LA &nstatue &+Lof an o&nl&+Wd &+Cman &+Lstands here in the center of the room.&n
~
&+L   This statue seems very old, and must have been built at the same time or
&+Labout the same time the tower was. The man seems to be human, and stands
&+Labout five and a half feet tall. He is stooped over slightly and carries a
&+Llong staff in his hands. He is dressed in long flowing robes that drape the
&+Lground. His features are carved out of the rock to make him look very hard,
&+Land a little mean. Carved into the base of the statue are the following words.

         If you are reading this then my dreams have worked.
      Know that I am Earlion De'Arthri, and I serve the
      Dark Lord Sargon. They came last week, Amrothlin, and
      Devylin with the others and imprisoned my god. The army
      Rose up upon them and slew some of their number, but
      the rest of them fled. Soon they will be here with the
      Goddess and she will destroy the Black Tower, and do
      Away with everything we hold dear, and if the Black
      Tower is destroyed all hopes of raising our master
      are gone. Therefore I have sealed the Tower away in
      The place which Is Not and cannot Be. One day someone
      Will come and free the Tower, until then, I who cast
      the spell must stay within the Tower, unable to age
      or die. I Shall seal myself away in my chambers to
      the north. Know that I have one of the keys of the Star
      Stone. Go into your separate picture portals my brothers
      and retrieve the keys I have placed there to open
      up my stasis should you have need of me or the Key.&n
~
