&+yThe &+mT&+Mukluk &n&+wC&+Whief &N&+ywonders how he can possibly defeat the Butsus.&N
~
&+yIn a time long ago, the twenty most faithful worshipers of &+rM'Bele &+ywere each
&+ygranted their own tribe and told that the last surviving chieftain would be
&+ygiven the powers of &+rM'Bele &+yhimself. Six were killed within a day, during the
&+ychaos that followed such a titanic announcement; the others began claiming
&+yterritory and making plans for their eventual victory. By the time the number
&+yof tribes had been whittled to ten, thirty years had passed, and the other
&+yten chieftains realized that they were immune to the effects of aging. In
&+ythe centuries since then, eight more of the contestants have met with the
&+yspear-point of an enemy, until now only two chieftains are left. Soon enough
&+ythe competition will end, and &+rM'Bele &+ywill once again walk the earth, wetting
&+yit with the blood of warriors and innocents alike.&N
~
